answer 92% or 93% of the time,

84
00:04:29.412 --> 00:04:33.882
then you do need a larger
set of examples to measure those

85
00:04:33.882 --> 00:04:36.117
differences between 91%
and 93% performance.

86
00:04:36.117 --> 00:04:36.117


87
00:04:36.738 --> 00:04:41.293
And then only if you really need an
unbiased, fair estimate of how

88
00:04:41.293 --> 00:04:44.446
was the system doing,
then do you need to

89
00:04:44.446 --> 00:04:49.001
go beyond the development set
to also collect a hold-out test set. One

90
00:04:49.001 --> 00:04:51.804
important caveat, I've seen
